                "top" : {
                  "unit" : "px",
                  "value" : 10.0
                }
              },
              "lightning:typography" : "{!$brand.typography.paragraph.paragraph1}",
              "text" : "Market Availability starts with occupied beds as a proxy for market demand, then burns down as beds are pre-leased through the cycle. Capture Rate shows the share of the market’s remaining available beds your property would need to sign to reach 100% pre-lease. Both run against prior cycles, so you can see whether you’re leasing faster or slower than the market.<br />For developers, the pipeline view puts beds in lease-up, under construction, and planned next to performance in the same market. <br /><br /><strong><em>If your team relies on broker calls and a general CRE data subscription today, College House fits alongside both. It adds weekly, floor plan-level student housing data that neither provides. </em></strong>"
